WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:06.370
From an alternate Zurg twist, to a monkey
version of Sox, and even more Pizza Planet

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:10.210
easter eggs, Pixar's Lightyear was originally
a very different movie!

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:14.650
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing everything Pixar

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.760
deleted from Lightyear.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.660
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:23.119
The big twist in Lightyear comes when the
identity of Zurg is revealed and it turns

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:26.789
out he's an older version of Buzz from an
alternate timeline.

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:31.759
When Buzz finally achieved 100% hyperspeed,
the event split the timeline – notice these

00:00:31.759 --> 00:00:34.870
two bursts of energy which occur at that very
moment.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:39.559
The second Buzz travelled centuries into the
future and discovered a ship with advanced

00:00:39.559 --> 00:00:44.860
alien technology, an enormous mecha robot
suit, and Zyclops robots who mispronounced

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.449
his name as Zurg.

00:00:46.449 --> 00:00:52.579
But when older Buzz, aka Zurg, opens his robot
"suit", main timeline Buzz initially mistakes

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:55.840
him for his father because of his similar
but aged features.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.670
Originally, Pixar planned for the twist in
Lightyear to be that Zurg had indeed been

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:05.309
Buzz's father all along, which would have
matched the same reveal in Toy Story 2.

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:06.560
You killed my father!

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.130
No, Buzz.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:11.270
I AM your father.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.270
No!

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.299
Director Angus MacLane explained that during
the movie's development, they spent a lot

00:01:16.299 --> 00:01:21.290
of time laying the groundwork and hints to
the big reveal that Zurg was in fact Buzz's

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:22.290
dad.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:27.869
But when the payoff came, it felt incredibly
unsatisfying, because it was too obvious from

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:32.170
all the clues that had been teased for at
least the first hour of the movie.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:37.280
On top of that, there was the fact that everyone
who'd ever seen Toy Story 2 knew this twist

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.939
about Zurg had already been played as a Star
Wars joke in that movie.

00:01:41.939 --> 00:01:46.730
So, in the end, MacLane decided it would be
more interesting if the twist was that Zurg

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:51.340
was a version of Buzz himself, but one that
went on a different, darker path.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.640
So, Buzz turns out to basically be his own
worst enemy.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:00.189
The director said he was inspired by Indiana
Jones And Raiders of the Lost Ark where the

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:05.259
French archaeologist who works with the Nazis
tells Indy that he's just a slightly different

00:02:05.259 --> 00:02:06.259
version of him.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:08.220
I am a shadowy reflection of you.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.530
It would take only a nudge to make you like
me.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:15.381
I can see that having Zurg as Buzz's father
would have been way too predictable, and the

00:02:15.381 --> 00:02:21.040
Disney animated series Buzz Lightyear of Star
Command already spoofed the Toy Story 2 revelation

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.319
in favour of making Zurg a straight-up villain,
unrelated to Buzz…

00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:27.319
There's something you must know.

00:02:27.319 --> 00:02:29.940
I am your father.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:30.940
Psych!

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.860
Made you look, you dimwit!

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.890
…so Lightyear's filmmakers likely felt they
wanted to do something different to that particular

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.840
take in the new movie as well.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:45.620
A firm fan favourite in the new movie is the
hilarious, robotic cat Sox.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:46.620
Sox.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.620
Pfft.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.620
You're inhibiting my visuals.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:49.620
Oh, sorry, is this better?

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:50.620
Negative.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.620
OK, how about this.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:52.620
Pfft.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.430
But, originally, the filmmakers were going
to have a monkey as Buzz's cute animal sidekick

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:57.430
instead.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:01.890
The idea for a monkey came from how NASA and
other space agencies have sent monkeys and

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:05.680
other primates into space as part of research
into space travel.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.280
The filmmakers planned on having a type of
helper monkey who would assist Buzz on his

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.280
missions.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.600
In the end though they found a robotic cat
was funnier than a monkey…

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.030
Sox, how long were we gone?

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.480
Meow, meow, meow, meow, meow…

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:21.019
Bee-boop, Bee-boop, Bee-boop, Bee-boop, Bee-
…and so they ended up with Sox and his amusing

00:03:21.019 --> 00:03:23.250
animatronic style of movement and commentary.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.519
Buzz, that was utterly terrifying and I regret
having joined you.

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:30.920
The Pizza Planet truck and franchise, which
first appeared in Toy Story, has made an appearance

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.989
in almost every Pixar movie so far.

00:03:33.989 --> 00:03:38.250
Lightyear is no exception and a pizza delivery
vehicle makes a tricky-to-spot cameo in the

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:42.040
scene where Buzz and Sox are fleeing the Star
Command police.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:46.710
As they drive down the highway you can see
the iconic Pizza Planet rocket on top of a

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:49.930
truck parked up, and a guy delivering some
pizzas.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:54.930
But originally, as we can see from this unused
concept art, there were also plans to show

00:03:54.930 --> 00:04:00.000
scenes with Pizza Planet stores and locations
on the new planet, giving us more of an insight

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.810
into the layout of this new world and how
people were living there.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:08.379
And apparently in another deleted scene, Buzz
would have "gone grocery shopping" after he

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:10.560
ran out of his pre-assigned meals.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.860
There was going to be a joke where Buzz asked
for a packet of "dinner" - like the meal boxes

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:19.730
he was used to eating -, but after his many
years away, food has changed and he ended

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:25.490
up being sold something called "pobbles" which
MacLane described as "spiky, space" food.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:30.870
The concept art also has some references to
the green aliens who Buzz first met at Pizza

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.500
Planet in Toy Story.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.260
Who's in charge here?

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:36.390
The claw!

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:40.580
Some fans have been disappointed they didn't
make an appearance in Lightyear, especially

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:44.750
as some of the Little Green Men worked for
Star Command in the animated series.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:49.070
However, MacLane has explained that he didn't
think it made sense for them to appear in

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:53.450
Lightyear, a movie that Andy saw before the
events of Toy Story.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:58.290
As the aliens don't know who Buzz is when
he pops up in their claw machine in Toy Story,

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:02.500
it fits that they shouldn't have met him previously
in the new prequel movie.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.700
MacLane has confirmed though that there is
an easter egg to the squeeze-toy aliens in

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:11.050
the first mid-credits scene, where you can
see a little statue of one of the green men

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.200
on Commander Burnside's shelf.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:17.810
And, if you're a fan of the hilarious Little
Green Men or you're enjoying this video so

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:20.810
far, do leave a thumbs-up, I really appreciate
it.

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:25.830
When Zurg confronts Buzz for the first time
and corners him, Buzz is saved when the Junior

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.640
Zap Patrol blast the villain to the floor.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:33.590
As Zurg recovers, he uses his arm controls
to call on a team of Zyclops to help him trap

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:34.590
Buzz.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:39.220
The original storyboard for this sequence
reveals a hilarious little deleted moment

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:43.750
where the Zurg-bots can be seen chilling out
in a lounge on the ship, playing cards and

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:48.120
pool together, just before Zurg's command
activates them.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:52.862
Also cut from the final movie was a scene
involving a killer robot hound that Zurg had

00:05:52.862 --> 00:05:54.900
sent to hunt Buzz in the future.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:59.590
In this deleted rainy action sequence, which
has shades of Blade Runner, Buzz would have

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:05.100
had a special briefcase with a weapon though
it completely failed to stop the canine antagonist

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:09.250
and he ended up getting caught by the robot
dog.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:13.670
Lightyear also made some significant changes
to Zurg's design compared to the Toy Story

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:14.670
movies.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:20.140
This Zurg is more robot-like, influenced by
anime and mecha, and his huge size was intended

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:23.060
to make him incredibly intimidating.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:28.530
This more robotic look also meant Pixar ditched
the cape Zurg wore in Toy Story 2.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:29.530
No capes!

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:34.520
Losing Zurg's colourful cape, however, meant
this version of the villain was heavy on purple

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:39.060
and The Art of Lightyear book reveals some
of Zurg's early designs which included a lot

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.980
of red and other colours.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:46.480
These were discarded eventually and instead
red accents were given to Zurg via decals,

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:48.050
pinstripes and labels.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:52.320
Zurg's horns were also reduced in size to
appear "less devil-like".

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:58.090
And this Zurg also got an enormous extendable
hand, akin to a claw, possibly a nod to the

00:06:58.090 --> 00:07:00.300
Little Green Men from Toy Story.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.430
The claw!

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:07.580
The Art of Lightyear book also reveals some
interesting alternate designs for Commander

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:11.640
Burnside where he had a bionic arm, which
implies there's an interesting backstory for

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:13.910
Burnside that we didn't get to see.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:18.370
Curiously enough, there was also another character
with a bionic arm who ended up cut from the

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.370
film.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:24.620
As well as scrapping a storyline which showed
how Buzz became a Space Ranger in the first

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:29.720
place, and a sequence which featured him ending
up in a Star Command brig over rivalry and

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:34.610
insults, the Art of Lightyear book also reveals
a lot of deleted characters that never made

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:36.330
it into the final movie.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:40.830
There were some Miyazaki-inspired helper machines
called Minerbots that would have presumably

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:45.550
appeared when Buzz and the Zap Patrol went
to the mining plant on the dark side of the

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:46.550
planet.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:51.270
There are also all of these unused characters
which the concept art book reveals as being

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.580
"Out of Picture".

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:56.740
And if you'd like to get a copy of The Art
of Lightyear with all of these cool designs,

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:01.150
and a lot more concept art, including the
original designs for Buzz Lightyear, before

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:05.680
Toy Story, when he was called Lunar Larry,
you can tap here to get the book with free

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:06.980
